H71 traced fourteen selected source units in the pinned public framework. Prompt masking uses the length of a separately templated prefix and needs actual prefix/target validation. The batching code pads with zeros and truncates lengths; the selected loss uses an inclusive upper length. H72 independently projected the indices for six synthetic conditions using owned integer arithmetic. In the short masked example, positions4–8 are selected although only4–7 belong to the original target; position8 is zero-filled padding. Other cases show zero supervision after full target truncation, positive supervision after partial truncation, and a positive count consisting only of padding. These are source-bound index findings, not observed MLX loss values, NaNs, training crashes or a framework failure rate. No framework or tokenizer was imported or executed.

